  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.8: Continues the preview.6/preview.7 fail-closed hardening pass with one targeted security fix surfaced by the new Stryker.NET mutation-testing layer. SECURITY: a token whose `exp` claim sat exactly at UnixSecondsMax (DateTimeOffset.MaxValue.ToUnixTimeSeconds()) escaped Validate as a raw ArgumentOutOfRangeException from `exp + skew` overflowing DateTimeOffset.MaxValue — a fail-closed totality violation. The symmetric underflow existed for `nbf - skew` at UnixSecondsMin. Both sites now clamp the arithmetic: `exp` past max-minus-skew is effectively infinite (check passes by definition); `nbf` below min-plus-skew is symmetric. Regression-locked by 11 new BoundaryTests.cs cases. Tokens produced by this library's builder are unaffected; the public API and wire format are unchanged. Also added: Stryker.NET mutation-testing scaffold (66.31% raw / ~87% on behaviorally-meaningful mutations after filtering exception-message String survivors), a named red-team scenario suite (RedTeamScenarios.cs), and reviewer-facing docs (docs/TESTING.md, docs/SUPPLY-CHAIN.md, docs/ROADMAP-TO-1.0.md). Production-oriented preview: NOT independently audited, NOT a drop-in OAuth/OIDC/JWT replacement. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
